msgid ""
"Everything you might want to know before sending your first future letter."
msgstr ""
"Все, что обычно интересует пользователей перед отправкой их первого письма в "
"будущее."

#: letters/templates/letters/faq.html:29
msgid "1. How much does LetterGator cost, and when is it charged?"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/faq.html:34
msgid ""
"Scheduling a letter for under 1 year is free. For schedules at 1 year or "
"beyond, the price is $0.50 per year. The total is charged once when you "
"click Seal and Store, not every month. You can always write letters without "
"paying; payment is only required for long-term scheduling. To unlock 1 year+ "
"scheduling options, keep at least $1.00 in your balance."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/faq.html:46
msgid "2. How reliable is delivery, and what backup details can I provide?"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/faq.html:51
msgid ""
"LetterGator is built for reliable future delivery with retry logic if a "
"first attempt fails. You can send to yourself or to other recipients, and "
"add up to 5 recipient emails. For additional account-level safety, you may "
"provide a phone number and address in your profile. If provided, those "
"details help us keep your account contact information complete for "
"exceptional support and verification situations."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/faq.html:64
msgid "3. Can I change, delete, or preview a letter after I create it?"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/faq.html:69
msgid ""
"You control this at creation time. If you enable Allow Edit and/or Allow "
"Delete, those actions are available only during the first 30 days after the "
"letter is created. If you leave either option disabled, that action is not "
"available after creation at all. Message preview works the same way: if See "
"Message Before Delivery is enabled, you can view your content before "
"delivery; if disabled, the content stays sealed until delivery."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/faq.html:82
msgid "4. How do you make sure my email is still valid in future years?"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/faq.html:87
msgid ""
"To keep long-term delivery dependable, we send a re-confirmation email "
"roughly once a year so you can confirm your address and stay connected with "
"us. This also acts as a reminder to update your account details if your "
"email changes. If you plan to switch email providers, you can update your "
"email in your profile and confirm the new address so future letters continue "
"to route correctly."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/faq.html:100
msgid ""
"5. Is my message content private, and what happens if your database is lost?"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/faq.html:105
msgid ""
"Every message is encrypted before it is stored. The content is unreadable to "
"anyone who has access to our database — it can only be decrypted at the "
"moment of delivery. For permanent resilience, the encrypted message data is "
"also written to Arweave — a decentralised blockchain storage network built "
"to keep data available permanently. Even if our own database were ever lost "
"or destroyed, the encrypted letter data is preserved on the blockchain and "
"cannot disappear."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/faq.html:119
msgid "6. Can I attach files to a letter?"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/faq.html:124
msgid ""
"Not yet — letters currently support a rich text body only. File attachments "
"are planned for a near-future version. You will be able to attach videos, "
"audio recordings, images, and other files directly to your letter so the "
"recipient receives everything in one delivery. We will announce this feature "
"as soon as it is available."
msgstr ""

